※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4460

※ Which member is wanted decides what type the expression has, so it has to be
※ known while compiling.  An index the program works out would leave the type to
※ be settled while it runs, which no type in this language is.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let p: 〈u8, u8〉 = 〈1u8, 2u8〉
    let at: u8 = 1u8
    p⟦at⟧
